-- Seed data for the tasks table — NOT a migration, don't number/apply this like one.
-- Run it manually via the Supabase SQL editor, AFTER seed-seasons.sql, seed-key-stages.sql
-- and seed-departments.sql, and after migrations 0015 and 0016 are applied.
--
-- Generated from `Critical Path - Data exported 24th August 2026.xlsx` (TASKS sheet), 833 rows
-- in, 793 out. The 40 that were dropped, and 35 more whose timeline was adjusted, are listed
-- with reasons in `seed-tasks-excluded.md` beside this file.
--
-- The season_id / key_stage_id / department_id values below are the REAL uuids read out of
-- this project's database at generation time, not subqueries — re-generate this file if you
-- ever re-seed those lookups, or every FK here goes stale.
--
-- Task ids are uuid5-derived from (season, task name, sheet row), so regenerating produces
-- byte-identical ids and a re-run replaces rather than duplicates.
--
-- Fields the sheet does not carry, and what they were set to:
--   brand_id   null — the export has no BRAND column at all (brand is only implied by a few
--              season names like "RIP CURL Q3'26"). Nullable since 0016_tasks_brand_optional.
--   gender     'unisex' — no column in the sheet; this is the neutral default, not a guess at
--              the real value.
--   status     'not_started' for every row. The sheet's "X" column looked like a completion
--              marker but does not behave as one (166 future-dated tasks carry it, 63 past-due
--              tasks don't), so it is deliberately ignored rather than guessed at.
--   priority   'med' — the table default; the sheet has no priority column.
--   due_date   DUE DATE, falling back to "Due Date (zapier)" then "Working Timeline - End".
--   notes      NOTES, with the LINK cell appended as a "Link:" line including the real
--              hyperlink target pulled from the sheet's relationships, where one exists.
--
-- Owners and People Involved both land in task_participants as DEPARTMENTS — every party in
-- the export maps to a department except one individual (see the exclusions file).

begin;

